# Audio hitch check: the moments audio starts heavy work must not cost the main
# thread a frame. At Riverwood, with the region ambience, emitters and explore music already playing:
# - a music type change that starts a streamed track (MUSCombat, ducking the explore music);
# - four dialogue lines started in one frame (their files read and decoded on the loader thread);
# - a burst of 64 positioned one-shots in one frame (combat and physics impacts around the camera).
# Needs the sounds imported (the import cache's audio, or %LOCALAPPDATA%\spud\cache\audio).
name audio-load
world tamriel
resolution 2560 1440
draw_distance 12
start 19420 -44746 -109 57 0
segment music-start
audio music add MUSCombat
hold 0.8
segment voices
audio playfile sound/voice/skyrim.esm/malenord/dialoguewh__0003a145_1.ogg AudioCategoryVOCGeneral SOMDialogue3DDefault here
audio playfile sound/voice/skyrim.esm/malenord/dialoguewh__0003a14a_1.ogg AudioCategoryVOCGeneral SOMDialogue3DDefault here
audio playfile sound/voice/skyrim.esm/malenord/dialoguewh__0003b2c0_1.ogg AudioCategoryVOCGeneral SOMDialogue3DDefault here
audio playfile sound/voice/skyrim.esm/malenord/dialoguewh__0003a154_1.ogg AudioCategoryVOCGeneral SOMDialogue3DDefault here
hold 0.8
segment burst
audio playrel WPNImpactBladeVsIceSD 150 0 0
audio playrel WPNSwingBladeMediumSD 189 19 20
audio playrel WPNImpactBladeVsArmorSD 226 45 40
audio playrel WPNImpactBladeVsFleshSD 258 78 60
audio playrel WPNImpactBladeVsDirtSD 286 119 80
